.TH DAMI 1 "August 2026" "Dami Core" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dami \- trace-first personal assistant runtime, from the shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dami
.I verb
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every consequential operation is a durable, replayable event. What the commands
print is rendered from the persisted stream \- the display invents nothing.
.SH SURFACINGS
.TP
.B dami inbox
Pending surfacings, newest first. The default when no verb is given.
.TP
.B dami recent
Recently delivered surfacings.
.TP
.B dami read \fIid8\fR
Read one surfacing in full and mark it delivered.
.TP
.B dami good\fR|\fBbad\fR|\fBmeh \fIid8\fR [\fInote\fR]
React. Reactions feed the taste model and tune the surfacing threshold.
.SH MEMORY AND BELIEFS
.TP
.B dami recall \fIquery\fR
Semantic recall over the observation corpus.
.TP
.B dami beliefs \fR[\fIdate\fR]
The active belief ledger, or the ledger as of a date.
.TP
.B dami retract \fIid8\fR \fIreason\fR
Retract a belief. The retraction is durable; the vector goes with it.
.TP
.B dami note \fItext\fR
Append an observation by hand.
.SH TURNS
.TP
.B dami chat \fImessage\fR
One full interactive turn: context, routing, local model, traced.
.TP
.B dami chat --frontier \fImessage\fR
The same turn answered by your ChatGPT subscription through the codex
CLI \- no API key, no billing. Dami's identity is sent; your memories
are not. For a memory-informed frontier answer use \fBdami brief\fR.
.TP
.B dami ask \fIquestion\fR
A lighter question against the local model with retrieved context.
.TP
.B dami context \fIrequest\fR
Show exactly what would enter the prompt, and its token cost.
.TP
.B dami caption \fIimage\fR
Caption an image with the local vision model, run as a bounded worker
under a real trace. The image never leaves the host.
.SH SESSIONS
.TP
.B dami sessions
List recent durable conversations, newest activity first.
.TP
.B dami session start \fR[\fIid\fR]
Start an active session. The CLI creates a stable client ID when omitted.
.TP
.B dami session resume \fIid\fR
Resume an interrupted session.
.TP
.B dami session interrupt \fIid\fR
Interrupt the session and atomically interrupt any running turn.
.TP
.B dami session turn \fIid\fR \fImessage\fR
Run one context-bearing turn. The request ID prints before the network call so it
survives an SSH disconnect.
.TP
.B dami session reconnect \fIid\fR \fIrequest-id\fR
Read the durable state and response without re-executing the request.
.SH FRONTIER
.TP
.B dami frontier \fIquestion\fR
A bare question to the frontier via the codex subscription. No memories
are sent (ADR-0011).
.TP
.B dami brief \fIquestion\fR
Draft a redacted, memory-informed brief. The exact bytes print for review
and egress only after \fBdami approve\fR (ADR-0013: consent is the transform).
.SH APPROVALS
.TP
.B dami approvals
Pending approvals.
.TP
.B dami approve \fIid8\fR
Approve and execute: librarian manifests move files; frontier briefs egress.
.TP
.B dami deny \fIid8\fR [\fIreason\fR]
Deny. It never runs.
.SH OPERATIONS
.TP
.B dami trace \fIid\fR
Replay one trace, child spans indented. Accepts the 8-char short ids
other commands print.
.TP
.B dami health
Service health, including the GPU-residency check for the LLM sidecar
and the runtime API.
.TP
.B dami health-log
The structured health timeline extracted from your own notes (K2).
Local only \- these rows have no egress path.
.TP
.B dami stats
Corpus and event-stream counts.
.TP
.B dami board \fR[\fIboard\fR [--open]]
The collaborative task board (O1). Alone, lists boards; with a board id or
title prefix, prints its task tree with 8-char ids, status marks, and
claimants. \fB--open\fR hides finished work.
.TP
.B dami board claim|complete \fIid8\fR [\fInote\fR]
Claim a task, or complete one you hold. Acts as \fB$DAMI_ACTOR\fR
(kind \fB$DAMI_ACTOR_KIND\fR, Human or Agent; default: the login user,
Human). A 409 from the board is reported as a conflict, never retried.
.TP
.B dami board block|reopen|cancel \fIid8\fR \fIreason\fR
Change a task's status with a recorded reason.
.TP
.B dami board criterion \fIid8\fR yes|no
Mark an acceptance criterion satisfied or not.
.TP
.B dami board needs \fIid8\fR \fIcriterion\fR
Add an acceptance criterion to an unfinished task. Completion will not pass
until it is marked satisfied.
.TP
.B dami board add \fIid8\fR|\fIboard\fR \fItitle\fR [--needs \fIcriterion\fR]...
Add a task under a task, or at a board's root, last among its siblings.
Each \fB--needs\fR becomes an acceptance criterion the completion gate
checks. The title starts with the task's id (\fBO2g Do the thing\fR); on
the suite board that id is the task's identity in TODO.md too. Adding under
a finished task reopens it, on the record.
.TP
.B dami board export \fIboard\fR
Print the board in TODO.md's own grammar. What the grammar cannot say is
written as an HTML comment, never invented into a task.
.TP
.B dami board-import \fITODO.md\fR --revision \fIsha\fR --actor \fIid\fR [--agent] [--dry-run]
Write the blueprint onto the collaborative task board (O1g). Talks to
PostgreSQL directly. Safe to rerun: it only advances tasks, and where the
board already knows better than the file it reports the conflict and
leaves the board alone. \fB--dry-run\fR prints the plan and anomalies
without writing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/dami/cli
The published CLI. \fI/usr/local/bin/dami\fR points here.
.TP
.I ~/dev/dami-agent/docs/
Charter, architecture, decision records, runbook.
.SH SEE ALSO
The work log and status board in \fIdocs/\fR are the running record.
